    {
      "@type": "FAQPage",
      "mainEntity": [
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What types of notices does ROC Pune issue?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "ROC Pune issues several types of notices under the Companies Act, 2013: strike-off notices under Section 248 (Form STK-1) for non-filing of annual returns, adjudication penalty notices under Section 454 for specific statutory violations, director disqualification communications under Section 164(2), and deficiency/resubmission notices for incorrect filings. Since the February 2026 MCA reform, ROC Pune has expanded adjudication powers for minor violations."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How do I reply to a ROC notice in Pune?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "File all pending annual returns (AOC-4, MGT-7, DIR-3 KYC, ADT-1) on mca.gov.in with applicable additional fees. Prepare a written representation addressed to ROC Pune explaining the reasons for default and confirming compliance. Attach board resolution and copies of filed forms. Submit within 30 days. If the CCFS 2026 window is open, file under the scheme for reduced fees and penalty immunity."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What is CCFS 2026 and how does it help?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "CCFS 2026 (Companies Compliance Facilitation Scheme 2026) is a one-time compliance relief programme launched by MCA via General Circular 01/2026 on 24 February 2026. The scheme window runs from 15 April to 15 July 2026. Companies with pending annual filings can file at reduced additional fees with conditional immunity from penalties. If filing is completed before an adjudication notice, no penalties apply."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Can a struck-off company be restored?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Yes. A struck-off company can be restored by filing an application under Section 252 before the NCLT Mumbai Bench within 3 years of the strike-off date. The applicant must demonstrate that the company was carrying on business at the time of strike-off or that restoration is just. All pending filings must be completed. The process takes 3-6 months."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Can directors be disqualified for ROC non-compliance?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Yes. Under Section 164(2), directors of companies that have not filed annual returns for any continuous period of three financial years are disqualified from appointment as director of any company for five years. Their DIN is deactivated across all companies. This particularly affects Pune startup founders serving as directors of multiple entities."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What is the penalty for non-filing of AOC-4 and MGT-7?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Additional fees of Rs 100 per day per form accrue from the due date until filing. There is no cap. For a company 3 years late on both AOC-4 and MGT-7, additional fees exceed Rs 2,00,000. Beyond fees, the company faces adjudication penalties under Section 454 and potential strike-off under Section 248."
          }
        }
      ]
    }
