<!-- SECTION 2: OVERVIEW / INTRO + TL;DR -->
<section class="content-section" id="overview-section">
    <div class="content-container">
        <div class="text-content">
            <h2 class="section-title">ROC Notice in Pune - Overview</h2>
            <div class="content-text">
                <div class="highlight-box" style="margin-bottom:20px;">
                    <p><strong>&#128204; TL;DR - ROC Notice in Pune Services at a Glance</strong></p>
                    <p>A ROC notice is a formal communication from the Registrar of Companies (ROC) Pune to a company or its directors under the Companies Act, 2013, triggered by non-filing of annual returns (AOC-4, MGT-7), non-commencement of business, or specific violations. Common types include strike-off notices under Section 248 (Form STK-1), adjudication penalty notices under Section 454, director disqualification under Section 164(2), and deficiency notices. Companies must reply within 30 days, file all pending returns, and submit a representation to ROC Pune.</p>
                </div>
                <p>Pune is home to tens of thousands of registered companies and LLPs - from Hinjewadi IT subsidiaries and Kharadi startup ventures to MIDC manufacturing units and Baner-based professional firms. ROC Pune, headquartered at PMT Building, Shivaji Nagar, administers compliance for all these entities. ROC Pune has been one of the most active registrars in India for issuing strike-off notices and adjudication orders. The February 2026 MCA reform further expanded RoC adjudication powers. Learn more about <a href="/roc-notice">ROC Notice services across India</a>.</p>
                <p>The CCFS 2026 (Companies Compliance Facilitation Scheme) launched in February 2026 offers a time-limited window (15 April - 15 July 2026) for companies to clear pending filings at reduced fees with conditional immunity from penalties. File returns on <a href="https://www.mca.gov.in" target="_blank" rel="noopener">MCA portal (mca.gov.in)</a>. For annual filing support, see <a href="#">Annual ROC Filing in Pune</a> and <a href="#">Annual ROC Filing (India)</a>.</p>
                <p>Content is reviewed quarterly for accuracy.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<!-- SECTION 3: WHAT IS GSTAT APPEAL FILING -->
<section class="content-section" id="what-section">
    <div class="content-container">
        <div class="two-column">
            <div class="column-content">
                <h2 class="section-title">Types of ROC Notices</h2>
                <div class="content-text what-is-definition">
                    
                    <p><strong>Strike-Off Notice (Section 248, Form STK-1)</strong> - Issued when a company has not filed AOC-4 and MGT-7 for two consecutive years, or has not commenced business within one year. Company has 30 days to respond with representation and file all pending returns. Related: <a href="#">Company Strike Off</a>.</p><p><strong>Adjudication Penalty Notice (Section 454)</strong> - Issued for specific violations (CSR, SBO, auditor non-appointment). Following the February 2026 reform, ROC Pune has expanded independent adjudication powers. Penalties range from Rs 10,000 to Rs 1,00,00,000.</p><p><strong>Director Disqualification (Section 164/167)</strong> - Directors of companies with 3 consecutive years of non-filing are disqualified for 5 years. DIN deactivated across all companies. Impacts Pune startup founders on multiple boards.</p><p><strong>CCFS 2026 Opportunity (General Circular 01/2026)</strong> - Filing window 15 April - 15 July 2026. Reduced additional fees. Conditional immunity: no penalty if filing completed before adjudication notice.</p>

                </div>
                <div class="highlight-box" style="margin-top:20px;">
                    <p><strong>Key Terms for ROC Notice in Pune:</strong></p>
                    <ul><li><strong>Section 248 Strike-Off:</strong> ROC removes company for non-filing (2 years) or non-commencement (1 year)</li><li><strong>Section 454 Adjudication:</strong> ROC imposes penalties for statutory violations (Rs 10K to Rs 1 crore)</li><li><strong>CCFS 2026:</strong> MCA compliance relief scheme - 15 April to 15 July 2026 with reduced fees</li><li><strong>Section 164(2):</strong> Director disqualification for 5 years after 3 consecutive years of non-filing</li><li><strong>Form STK-1:</strong> Notice of proposed strike-off issued by ROC under Section 248</li><li><strong>Section 252:</strong> NCLT application for company restoration within 3 years of strike-off</li></ul>

                </div>
            </div>
