<section id="faq-section" class="content-section" style="background-color: #ffffff;">
    <div class="content-container">
        <div class="text-content">
            <div class="faq-expanded">
                <aside class="faq-expanded__aside">
                    <h2 class="faq-expanded__title">FAQs - ROC Notice in Pune</h2>
                    <p class="faq-expanded__lead">Find answers to the most common questions about ROC notices in Pune.</p>
                    @include('partials.faq-enquiry-form', ['enquiryLocation' => 'Pune', 'enquiryService' => 'ROC Notice in Pune'])
                </aside>
                <div class="faq-expanded__list">
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-1">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">What types of notices does ROC Pune issue?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>ROC Pune issues several types of notices under the Companies Act, 2013: strike-off notices under Section 248 (Form STK-1) for non-filing of annual returns, adjudication penalty notices under Section 454 for specific statutory violations, director disqualification communications under Section 164(2), and deficiency/resubmission notices for incorrect filings. Since the February 2026 MCA reform, ROC Pune has expanded adjudication powers for minor violations.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-2">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">How do I reply to a ROC notice in Pune?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>File all pending annual returns (AOC-4, MGT-7, DIR-3 KYC, ADT-1) on mca.gov.in with applicable additional fees. Prepare a written representation addressed to ROC Pune explaining the reasons for default and confirming compliance. Attach board resolution and copies of filed forms. Submit within 30 days. If the CCFS 2026 window is open, file under the scheme for reduced fees and penalty immunity.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-3">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">What is CCFS 2026 and how does it help?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>CCFS 2026 (Companies Compliance Facilitation Scheme 2026) is a one-time compliance relief programme launched by MCA via General Circular 01/2026 on 24 February 2026. The scheme window runs from 15 April to 15 July 2026. Companies with pending annual filings can file at reduced additional fees with conditional immunity from penalties. If filing is completed before an adjudication notice, no penalties apply.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-4">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">Can a struck-off company be restored?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Yes. A struck-off company can be restored by filing an application under Section 252 before the NCLT Mumbai Bench within 3 years of the strike-off date. The applicant must demonstrate that the company was carrying on business at the time of strike-off or that restoration is just. All pending filings must be completed. The process takes 3-6 months.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-5">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">Can directors be disqualified for ROC non-compliance?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Yes. Under Section 164(2), directors of companies that have not filed annual returns for any continuous period of three financial years are disqualified from appointment as director of any company for five years. Their DIN is deactivated across all companies. This particularly affects Pune startup founders serving as directors of multiple entities.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-6">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">What is the penalty for non-filing of AOC-4 and MGT-7?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Additional fees of Rs 100 per day per form accrue from the due date until filing. There is no cap. For a company 3 years late on both AOC-4 and MGT-7, additional fees exceed Rs 2,00,000. Beyond fees, the company faces adjudication penalties under Section 454 and potential strike-off under Section 248.</p></div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>


            <!-- Quick Answers -->
            <div class="highlight-box" style="margin-top:32px;">
                <p><strong>Quick Answers</strong></p>
                <p><strong>ROC notice mila hai - kya karna chahiye?</strong> 30 din ke andar reply dena hoga. Pehle sab pending returns (AOC-4, MGT-7) file karo MCA portal pe. Phir written representation ROC Pune ko bhejo. CCFS 2026 ka fayda lo (15 April - 15 July 2026).</p><p><strong>Company strike off ho gayi - kya wapas aa sakti hai?</strong> Haan, 3 saal ke andar NCLT Mumbai Bench mein application file karo Section 252 ke under. Sab pending filings complete karo. 3-6 mahine lagta hai.</p><p><strong>Director ka DIN deactivate ho gaya?</strong> Pehle defaulting company ke sab pending returns file karo. Phir DIN reactivation ke liye apply karo. Kuch cases mein NCLT jaana padta hai.</p>

            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

